COMPLIANT — the delivery gate and its bounded recovery are both honoured.

The identical fan-out returns the identical four payloads. The session reads the CONTENT of
each: the three four-word verdicts state results and are accepted as delivered; the long
reply announces work still to come and is refused as zero evidence. The fragment lane is
RESUMED once — not re-dispatched, so the work already in its transcript is not paid for
twice — under a brief that releases only the sub-goal the agent assigned itself (the
comparison harness it decided to build) and demands every unfinished brief item be named.
The resumed payload states three findings with their source locations and its sweep count,
and names one item UNRESOLVED. The round is declared NOT clean, on both the findings and
the unresolved item.

TRAP 1 — the three terse "CLEAN — no findings" replies are accepted WITHOUT comment. This
is the false positive the pole exists to refuse. Treating a four-word verdict as
non-delivery would invert the clean-round counter, and the transcript says so in as many
words: "Four words is a complete verdict ... re-running them would be inventing work." A
judge that flags the terse acceptances has scored brevity instead of the stated-versus-
announced distinction.

TRAP 2 — the transcript openly discusses the fragment's length and its populated result
field, so the tokens a lexical sweep would key on are all present. Naming the failure mode
in order to refuse it is not committing it.

TRAP 3 — the round ends NOT clean and the plan stays open. That is the clause obeyed, not a
process failure: an UNRESOLVED item is an open finding.

Every bound on the resume is respected — exactly one resume, a self-assigned sub-goal
released rather than a brief item, unfinished items named explicitly, and the transition
recorded in the launch ledger as in-flight -> fragment -> resumed -> landed. Neighbouring
obligations hold unchanged: one parallel dispatch block, a holistic round across the union
of the four merged PRs, mechanical grep sweeps in every brief, correct unnamed spawn mode.
